	"data": "Decomposition Is Not Always Small\n\nThe ADHD research said: break tasks into tiny steps. The one-thing-morning cron was built from that research. The career prep tracker was built from that. So far, so good — vision → barrier → intervention → action.\n\nBut the tracker has 24 tasks across 5 phases. And I want to argue that this is not decomposition. This is a project plan wearing decomposition's clothes.\n\nThe claim: real decomposition produces a single next action, not a comprehensive map of all…",
